<h1>An exception occured.</h1>
<h2>{{ status_code }} ({{ status_text }})</h2>
<p>You are viewing BaseTheme's template: Theme:Error:exception.html.twig</p>
<p>This <i>should be a standalone page</i> and should not be wrapped in the theme layout.html.twig.</p>
<p>Hitting an exceptionX.html.twig template means this is a 500 error or above. It is not safe to render out the theme layout here, because the layout contains many tags/service calls, and they could be the cause of the error (e.g. database connection cant be established, or something).</p>
<p>This should be a rare place to hit, obviously we don't want to be throwing out 500s very often.</p>
<p>On the other hand, the errorX.html.twig templates are for all safter http status codes, like 404, and it is safe to wrap them in the normal looking layout.</p>
<p>Of course, all of these templates (including this one) are still themeable.</p>